# PII name list for scripts/check-pii.sh (LOCAL - do not commit the real one).
#
# Copy this file to `.pii-names.local` and replace the placeholders with the
# actual customer/tenant names that must never appear in public artifacts.
# `.pii-names.local` is gitignored so the real names never enter the repo.
#
# Format: one name per line. Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
# Matching is case-insensitive, whole-word, and fixed-string (regex
# metacharacters in a name are matched literally, not interpreted).
#
# Only list CUSTOMER/TENANT names. Do NOT add your own org or product names
# (Strike48, Devo): they appear throughout the repo legitimately, so banning
# them would flag nearly every commit and PR. Prefer a distinctive full name
# over a short token (e.g. "TE Connectivity", not "TE").
#
# To push this list to CI, run `just pii-sync` (or scripts/set-pii-names.sh),
# which uploads it to the $PII_NAMES secret - see .github/workflows/pii-check.yml.
# Secrets are write-only, so re-run after every edit here.

example-customer-one
example-customer-two
